# fpga/CURRENT: the ONE resolver for the currently qualified FPGA packages.
#
# Consumers (template protocol T-fpga.4/5, T-snn.10, paper snapshot tooling)
# read this file instead of spelling a package path in prose: a version stored
# in prose drifts the next time the datapath is re-qualified, while this file
# travels with the repo state it describes. Update it in the same commit that
# qualifies a new package (tests/test_fpga_current.py checks every path).
#
# One block per problem class. polyhedral = rows plus box bounds, no cones;
# conic = rows and bounds plus native Euclidean-ball and scaled-SOC resets.
# On the board, v07 with cones off matches the v06 native emulation records on
# the v06 parity bundle (one-shot), 6x18 (one-shot, persistent), and 20x60 and
# 64x64 (one-shot). The polyhedral package is v08 (2026-10-11): it returns
# v06's raw state and telemetry byte for byte on the board (framework fixtures
# in both launch modes, forced STREAM/CG, and the economic-dispatch band fleet)
# and supersedes v06, which stays in the tree.
#
# Routing within the polyhedral class (measured 2026-10-23; full accounting
# in fpga/kv260_v08/evidence/regime_2026-10-23/). The class has two kernel
# generations on the board and the latency ranking flips with workload
# shape, so route by SHAPE and BOX SEMANTICS:
# - event-heavy (m small; tens to hundreds of projection events per outer
#   iteration, roughly >= 2n; the economic-dispatch band): v08, 2.9-8.0x
#   faster than v06 there.
# - matvec-heavy square (n = m; a handful of events per iteration, roughly
#   <= 10; the alt-investment horizons T = 16..80): v08 costs 2.1x the
#   cycles per outer iteration of the legacy row-interleave image (board app
#   snn_qp_solve, MAXN/MAXM 128) at equal board-verified 200 MHz, because
#   its resident matvecs issue 8 products/cycle against that image's 32.
#   v08 is still the default for NEW papers on this shape: it is the only
#   image carrying current (v0.5.0+) box-in-sweep semantics, and it still
#   beats one A53 core at every horizon (1.1-4.7x measured). The legacy
#   image implements the RETIRED pre-v0.5.0 box route (rows-only sweep,
#   clip after; a POCS failure the library fixed with facets-in-sweep) and
#   is reproduction-only for published numbers under matched-semantics
#   goldens, never a new paper's headline arm.
# - a square matvec-heavy paper whose headline needs a faster
#   current-semantics kernel is the trigger for the widened-matvec rebuild
#   (see the v08 README's regime-boundary section), not a route back to the
#   legacy image.
# Every measured polyhedral arm records n, m, and events per outer iteration
# beside the package name, and quotes the kernel clock as the clock record's
# kernel_hz_measured, never pl0_ref: on a clk_wiz app pl0_ref is the wizard
# INPUT (this package's board app runs pl0_ref 250 MHz through a 0.8 ratio
# to a true 200 MHz kernel clock).
#
# cpu_baseline: none means no qualified same-solver CPU harness exists for
# that class; extend and requalify one (T-snn.10 point 2).
polyhedral:
  package: fpga/kv260_v08
  boundary: fpga/kv260_v08/README.md
  cpu_baseline: fpga/cpu_baseline/cpu_baseline.cpp
  datapath_width_source: fpga/kv260_v08/src/dt.h
  qualified: 2026-10-11
conic:
  package: fpga/kv260_v07
  boundary: fpga/kv260_v07/README.md
  cpu_baseline: none
  datapath_width_source: fpga/kv260_v07/src/dt.h
  qualified: 2026-09-24
